<!--
  Robot configuration for the two-wheel pinch launcher test rig.

  THIS IS NOT A ROBOT. It is a bench rig on its own Control Hub, whose WiFi
  name is FTC-EoM3. It exists to characterize a launcher design with two
  side-by-side wheels that pinch the game piece between them.

  Like the robot configs, it ships inside the APK and appears in the Driver
  Station list as "robot_launcher_rig" as soon as the app is installed. The one
  manual step, once per hub: on the rig's Driver Station,
  Configure Robot -> robot_launcher_rig -> Activate. The Launcher2 Speed Test
  OpMode warns if some other configuration is active.

  WIRING - read before changing anything here:
  Both launcher motors (goBILDA Yellow Jacket 6000 RPM, 1:1, wheel on the
  shaft) share motor port 0 through a Y-cable, so they always receive the same
  power. Only one of the two encoders can be connected; it is on encoder
  port 0. Software therefore sees ONE motor, "launcher2", and its RPM is the
  speed of whichever motor's encoder is plugged in. The other wheel is assumed
  to match.

  The wheels turn opposite ways because of how the motors are mounted and
  wired, not because of anything in code. If one wheel turns the same way as
  the other, that is a wiring fix; no software setting can separate them.

  Device names here must match org.firstinspires.ftc.teamcode.hardware.DeviceNames
  (the LAUNCHER_RIG list). RobotConfigXmlTest fails the build if they disagree.
-->
<Robot type="FirstInspires-FTC">
    <LynxUsbDevice name="Control Hub Portal" serialNumber="(embedded)" parentModuleAddress="173">
        <LynxModule name="Control Hub" port="173">

            <!-- Both launcher motors, Y-cabled to one port. -->
            <goBILDA5202SeriesMotor name="launcher2" port="0" />

        </LynxModule>
    </LynxUsbDevice>
</Robot>
